WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.410
Reinforcements are on the way to the Solomon Islands.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.910
The Army and Navy will work together,

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.830
and crush the enemy in one decisive blow.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.330
Australia has also now become...

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.920
...fully cut off from its allies.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.840
In other words, it's an announcement from the Army HQ.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.050
I think the Ichiki's men probably went in...

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.970
...and were decimated.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.600
What exactly is going on?!

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.850
Isn't Guadalcanal going to remain in Allied hands?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.310
History has been altered, hasn't it?!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.690
It's true that there wasn't a second Battle of Guadalcanal.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.320
However, in our history books,

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.280
the submarine I-19 was the ship...

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.410
...that sunk the USS Wasp.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.120
Commander,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.830
permission's been granted for crew shore leave.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.370
The Navy has sent a message...

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.420
...granting us permission to go ashore tomorrow morning.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.670
We'll be under surveillance,

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.500
but we are free to move about within Yokosuka City.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.090
We really have to hand it to the great Mitsumasa Yonai.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.090
He really knows how to get things done.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.470
Once he decides on something, it gets done immediately.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.010
Oh, what a depressing color.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.140
Kohei, Masayuki.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.850
I need your help.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.690
The Place of Return

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.410
This is a little too fancy for me.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.620
Why am I the only one in uniform?!

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.200
You look fine.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.960
It's good that the color's not too flashy.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.500
It's a little tight,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.040
but I can't complain since it's a present.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.070
It's Yokosuka.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.700
We have returned at last.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.710
Debt,

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.710
War

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.710
and Victory!

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.710
Great East Asia Co-Prosperity Sphere

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.250
Just looking at the streets...

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.250
it gives me a strange feeling.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.920
It's something that we've only seen in photos,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.010
yet it feels like I've been here before.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.550
At the end of the day, we are Japanese...

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.300
and this is definitely Japan.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:06.350
Canteen Mikasa

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.140
Save Rice

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:07.470
Substitute
Foods

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.140
Look, "alternative" foods!

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.810
Tofu scraps instead of rice?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.850
It's a little early for lunch, but...

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.020
- Let's grab a bite.
- Yeah!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.740
Welcome.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.740
All clear. You can sneak out the back way.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.420
Alright, I'll be off.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.830
- I'll leave the rest to you.
- Yes.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.050
Watch out for the secret police.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.010
I'll be back by nightfall.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.300
Alright, let's just hang out here for as long as we can.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.510
We can get stuffed on "alternative" foods anyway.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.520
Menu: Substitute Food.
Mikasa Set Lunch

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.520
Madam, two Mikasa set lunches please!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.020
Fukagawa? I thought you were born in Kyushu?

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.740
I'm from Sasebo,

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.570
but my father was brought up in Fukagawa near Tokyo,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.280
and he should be 8 years old now.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.080
You're going to meet him?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.950
Yes, to clarify something.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.040
To make sure that this really is Japan,

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.290
and to find out what our connection is to this world.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.800
We'll help you lose our Navy escorts.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.550
Thank you.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.050
Tokyo

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.510
My grandfather was a carpenter and should be 36 years old now.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.060
My grandmother, a former geisha, is 32.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.140
My father... he should be around that boy's age.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.860
Mr. Yonai said that we're not part of this world,

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.570
but I don't agree.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.730
And I don't plan to be one either.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.950
I need something more to tie me...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.570
...to this world and the people of it.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.910
But what about Kusaka?

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.830
I don't know what his plans are after meeting Kanji Ishiwara,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.080
but whatever he's up to,

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.580
I know for sure he's trying to change things drastically.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.800
To Kusaka,

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.090
people aren't individuals, like the father and son sitting there.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.890
I'm the one who saved Kusaka and showed him the future,

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.310
so I am the one who will have to stop him.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:33.240
I heard that Fukagawa wasn't badly hit by the air raids.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.080
This place does look familiar.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.710
My father seldom went back to visit his old man though.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:41.500
I can count the number of times...

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.590
...he brought me back to see my grandfather on one hand.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.800
If that is Shintomichou Avenue...

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.760
Then it's just over there.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.720
Kadomatsu

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.690
That family's not in.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.910
I'll come again.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.370
Mourning

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.800
Sake    Oden    Tea

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.300
Welcome. It's hot, isn't it? Up to the 2nd floor please.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.310
- A glass of cold water please.
- Right away.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.730
Seven-all in the bottom of the 11th inning!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.900
Tokushima High has got a good chance to score some runs here!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.980
Heian High's pitcher just gave away back to back walks.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.780
Up to the plate steps Junichiro Suzuki,

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.320
he is 3 for 5 on the day with a double and 2 singles.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.820
- Here's the pitch...
- High school baseball...

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.620
Oh, they're still having the national finals?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.700
Shut that off! I don't want to listen to the radio!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.330
Damn, it's so boring!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.710
What in the world is that guy doing?

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:07.460
He's doing well in business?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.800
You've got to be kidding me.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.840
It's got to be something really sketchy...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.800
...if he's making money in a time like this!

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.850
I'm really sorry.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.140
That man's been on a bender since last night.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:21.980
It's best for you to ignore him if he tries to talk to you.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.140
Ok.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.230
That Yoichiro!

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.730
No matter what they say, he's still my son!

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.530
Yoichiro?!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.740
My dear son,

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.570
no matter where you are now,

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.990
you won't be embarrassed to have a carpenter as your father!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.750
Kadomatsu Yokichi!!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.120
That fool!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.180
He's my... grandfather?!

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.440
May I have a word with you?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.400
Huh? And who are you?!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.700
I'm just passing through.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.570
- Please.
- Oh.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.530
I see we're talking now.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.000
Are you Yokichi Kadomatsu, the carpenter?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.870
Yeah.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.420
I'm famous for...

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.500
...my fancy dressers, all my customers...

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.460
...love the darn things.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:37.260
I heard you talk about your son, Yoichiro.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.220
And what's it to you?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.600
Where is he now?

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.720
He's not here.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.020
Just because he's my older brother,

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:49.110
he thinks he can take away my only son?

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.730
What does he think he's doing? That creep!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.620
Father, can we go visit grandpa?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.620
Welcome aboard

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.620
It's pretty near from here, right?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.910
Yes, grandpa will be happy to see you.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.620
- You go ahead then.
- Come with me, Father.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.500
You're off work tomorrow, right?

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.750
If I go, we'll just end up fighting.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.630
But why?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.010
Your grandfather...

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:18.340
...still hasn't forgiven me for entering the Self-Defense Force.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.930
I think he hoped I would continue in his footsteps.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.850
I think your stubbornness...

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.270
...came from your grandfather.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.310
He's a skilled craftsman,

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.060
who hates to bow down to other people.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.070
And I heard from my father that he was...

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.860
...always getting into fights after drinking.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.650
His brother took my father in,

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.110
and raised him instead to provide a better environment.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.790
But then, you know what?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.960
I actually miss him!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.670
If you miss him,

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.460
then why don't you just go and bring him back?

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.380
Bring him back home,

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.170
and pass on your skills to him!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.840
Stop all this drinking and...

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.090
...use your energies to raise your son!

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.390
If I could do that,

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.970
I wouldn't be here now!

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.850
But why? You're his father right?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.520
I'm a father myself,

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.310
but a much better one than you!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.150
He's... no longer...

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.320
...alive!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.360
It's the Navy's fault!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.330
Darn it!!

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.830
That poor boy, Yoichiro.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:31.330
He was knocked down by a car on his way to the harbor.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.380
It happened 3 days ago.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.960
It was a naval officer's car.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.670
The funeral's today, but this man...

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:41.340
He's not even strong enough to attend his son's funeral.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.680
He may be good with his hands, but he's a drunk.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.350
What's going on?

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.650
My father is?

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.520
I always told him not to...

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.570
...go too near to the harbor.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:34.810
Please do not forget that you and your crew...

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.940
...are strangers in this era.

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.820
Mr. Kadomatsu,

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:41.690
you must make decisions based on the...

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.280
...future survival and prosperity of Japan!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.030
Everything may seem so nostalgic to us...

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.780
but this is not...

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.790
...the Japan that we came from!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.430
Who could it be at this hour?

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.440
I apologize for the late visit.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.310
But I need to speak with you now.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.320
That voice?!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:28.280
I apologize in advance for my poor hospitality.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.580
Your father is?

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.540
You mentioned that we are strangers here.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.550
And I disagreed with you on that.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.260
Even in this new history,

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.300
I believed that this was the world where I was born.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.470
However, this place is...

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:53.310
...a totally different reality from the Japan we came from.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.310
It's like a separate stream of history unfolding.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:14:00.900
In that case, will you stop meddling with history?

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.270
No.

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.280
Even if we were to stop now,

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.200
this world is not going to become what you hope it would be.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.280
There's someone out there who's actively making changes.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.790
Mr. Yonai,

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.660
can you please tell me where...

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.670
...former Navy Lieutenant, Takumi Kusaka, is?

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.210
I have never met that man before.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.800
But, I have an idea where he might be.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:30.720
Kanji Ishiwara invited me for some hotpot a few days ago.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.270
He was more excited than I've ever seen him.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.640
He was like a kid who found the key to the candy store.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.730
I'm guessing that it was Takumi Kusaka who put him...

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:45.900
...into that state by telling him what he knew of the future.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:50.570
That's him. I'm sure of it.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:54.410
In that case, Kusaka is no longer in Japan.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.260
Manchuria?!

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:16.270
In fact, I think he's probably in China now.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.100
What does he plan to do there?

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.770
I don't know what their plan is.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.440
But Ishiwara Kanji is the man who tried to make Manchuria...

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.110
...the United States of the Far East in the 1930s.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:30.820
It seems like their ambitions have been fused together.

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.610
To what end, I don't know.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.130
Will you chase him to Manchuria?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.760
If you're headed there,

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.890
I know someone in Shanghai who can help you.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.640
But Manchuria's far from there.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.600
I have responsibilities...

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.560
...as the second in command of the Mirai,

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.480
and I'm not supposed to be away from the ship for too long.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.530
However,

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.820
I was the one who let this man Kusaka learn what he knows.

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.780
I have to go out there and stop this man myself!

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.160
So you've made up your mind then?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.580
The longer I let him continue with his crazy plans,

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.130
the more lives will be lost.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.130
I'm not a stranger in this world.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.420
I'm just a normal person.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.420
And that is why I have to make Kusaka...

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.260
...come to his senses, and stop these...

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.890
...mad schemes of conquest whatever way I can.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.010
That's what I believe.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.970
A peace treaty with honor.

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.940
That's the 1st step to Zipang.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.100
Kusaka,

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.610
you're nothing but...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.570
...a normal man just like me.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.090
What do you think of the nice breeze?

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.050
Mr. Wang Tohai?

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.770
Indeed, a nice breeze indeed.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:41.950
I'm going to Manchuria.
Thanks for all you've done.
Take care.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.290
To that man,

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.000
defeat in war is alright as long as...

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.460
...the country recovers afterwards.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:53.460
But he also mentioned that a lost life can never come back.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.090
In just sixty years after the unconditional surrender,

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.470
the Japanese were able to fully recover.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.720
I'd have thought they would've needed more time than that.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:06.480
But in exchange, we will pay for that prosperity...

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.770
...with 3 million casualties from the war.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:15.320
Even if this nation is to fully recover,

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:19.360
even if she leaves her mark in history,

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.160
I...

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.580
...will be trapped in the flames of purgatory...

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.540
...forever.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.010
Prepare for refueling!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:43.310
I'm sorry you couldn't get any rest, Commander.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:47.140
No. I'm very sorry for acting out of line.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:50.100
Well, now you're going to do something...

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.520
...even more out of line, right?

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.360
In any case,

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.280
I'm surprised they granted us permission to dock so quickly.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.400
Of course, it wasn't without conditions.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.910
They want us to be under the Combined Fleet's command,

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.910
and to work together with them...

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.910
...in their war strategies.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.370
For the Mirai to survive in this era,

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.040
we have to follow their orders.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.750
That's right.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.670
However, I still have an ace up my sleeve.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.390
I've placed high-explosive bombs...

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.480
...all over the Mirai.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.390
They're all rigged up to...

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.690
...a remote device that...

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.900
...I had Kikuchi prepare for me.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.030
The largest bombs are next to the fuel tank.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:42.110
If the fuel goes up...

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.170
When did you do that?

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.880
While you were running around on land, Commander.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:01.050
With the push of a button, the Mirai can be erased.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.800
And perhaps the changes we've made to history...

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.800
...will be erased as well.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.890
This is the...

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.560
...final decision we have made.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.560
I fully support your decision!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.570
Will you go to Manchuria?

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:21.530
Yes, everything started with Kusaka and me.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.490
And everything won't be resolved until I confront and stop him.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.250
The Mirai has returned to Yokosuka.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.630
A ship has to go back to her home port.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.600
As a member of her crew,

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.190
you have to come back as well.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.610
The Mirai is your home port.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.280
Yes! Thank you very much!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:05.490
Yosuke, while you're away,

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.950
Kikuchi and I will protect the Mirai.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:10.040
Yosuke,

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.290
come back here with your faith restored!

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:24.510
Passing through the distant time

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:29.750
Just peacefully

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:41.560
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:54.440
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:21:54.940 --> 00:22:01.050
Not being able to do anything

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.120
I kept on praying

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:18.970
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:34.650
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:02.660
Kusaka, I'm going to find you!

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:24.930
Young man, where do you come from?

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:33.020
East from here,

00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:35.940
a beautiful country surrounded by the sea.

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:38.690
It's called... Zipang.

00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:45.120
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
